        "original_id": "a4206dee-c270-575b-bd90-07d4e04e4195",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Conan O'Brien, Robert Smigel, Brandon Tartikoff\n- Organizations: NBC\n- Projects: Lookwell\n- Roles: television executive, NBC president, creative voice\n\nFacts:\n- Brandon Tartikoff was an American television executive born on January 13, 1949, and he served as president of NBC from 1980 to 1991.\n- Lookwell was a television pilot written and produced by Conan O'Brien and Robert Smigel.\n- Robert Smigel later became a primary creative voice for Conan O'Brien's late night show.\n- Brandon Tartikoff considered Lookwell a personal favorite, but NBC did not pick up the pilot as a series.\n- Brandon Tartikoff died on August 27, 1997.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9ec6d44f-e662-5473-bb02-62eefe5487a5",
        "text": "Page: Lookwell. Sentence: Lookwell was a television pilot written and produced by Conan O'Brien and Robert Smigel, the latter of whom would become a primary creative voice for O'Brien's late night show.\nPage: Lookwell. Sentence: Despite being a \"personal favorite\" of NBC chairman Brandon Tartikoff, the pilot was not picked up as a series.\nPage: Brandon Tartikoff. Sentence: Brandon Tartikoff (January 13, 1949 – August 27, 1997) was an American television executive who was the president of NBC from 1980 to 1991.",
